# Commit message template for Adaptive Trust-Aware Medical RAG
#
# Format: <type>(<scope>): <short summary>
#
# Types:
#   feat      — New feature or pipeline component
#   fix       — Bug fix
#   chore     — Build, config, or infrastructure changes
#   docs      — Documentation only
#   test      — Adding or updating tests
#   refactor  — Code change that is not a fix or feature
#   perf      — Performance improvement
#   security  — Security hardening or vulnerability fix
#   eval      — Evaluation dataset, metrics, or experiment tracking
#   data      — Data ingestion, provenance, or schema changes
#
# Scopes (examples):
#   ingestion, trust-engine, retrieval, gates, normalization,
#   evaluation, hooks, rules, skills, schema, api, frontend
#
# Security checklist (complete before committing):
#   [ ] No hardcoded API keys, passwords, or tokens
#   [ ] No real patient data (PHI/PII)
#   [ ] No .venv, .env, or cache files
#   [ ] Gitleaks passed (Phase 4+)
#   [ ] Bandit passed (Phase 4+)
#
# Example:
#   feat(trust-engine): add adaptive weighting for R3 risk tier
#
#   Implements per-risk-class weight configuration via config/trust.yaml.
#   Adds unit tests for all four risk tiers.
#   Closes #12
